---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Likutay Aitzos - Hisbodidus" description="Likutay Aitzos - A Collection of Remedies and Advice on Hisbodidus from Rebbe Nachman of Breslov">
  <div class="book-page">
    <header class="book-header">
      <h1>Likutay Aitzos</h1>
      <h2>Hisbodidus - Alone Time</h2>
      <p class="subtitle">A Collection of Remedies and Advice from Rebbe Nachman of Breslov</p>
    </header>

    <div class="intro-section">
      <p>Likutay Aitzos presents succinct summations of the teachings of Rabbi Nachman in such a way that they can be readily and practically implemented. Rabbi Nachman himself commissioned Rabbi Nussun to compose it.</p>
      <p>Hisbodidus (pronounced: hisboadidoos) literally means to be alone, and it takes on the meaning and function of all things holy that are best, or can only be achieved, alone.</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="toc">
      <h3>Table of Contents</h3>
      <ol class="chapter-list">
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch01">Hisbodidus is a gateway to the Secrets of the Torah</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch02">Personal words to G-d are Divinely inspired</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch03">Yearning creates potential souls, verbalizing the yearning actualizes them</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch04">Connect the heart to its point to save it from the shame of fallen desires</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch05">Speaking to G-d will bring one to be embarrassed before Him with such holy connection that his face will shine</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch06">Abnegation to be included in one's root</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch07">At night, go alone to somewhere people never go, and completely nullify yourself to G-d</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch08">Hisbodidus at night, crying to G-d and building ones good points from out of the bad, bring joy, and holds lust at bay</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch09">Sighing – to regain one's standing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch10">G-d helps and provides words for one to prevail and be victorious despite all</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch11">Candidly unburdening oneself to G-d evokes Divine consolation</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch12">Do hisbodidus in the fields</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch13">Highest virtue, Speak in your vernacular, and Set a designated hour daily</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch14">Pray to attain what you learned</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch15">Trying to cry is also a distraction</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch16">Hisbodidus is the only way to succeed</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch17">Find yourself in the Psalms and prayers</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch18">Speak even without heart, always start new</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch19">Speak to Hashem until your soul is about to depart</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch20">Speak to Hashem like you speak to a friend</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch21">Speak to G-d like an enamored toddler pesters his father</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch22">Scream silently</a></li>
        <li><a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch23">A Broken Heart Is Precious and Not Sadness</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="book-nav">
      <a href="/books" class="back-link">← Back to Books</a>
      <a href="/books/likutay-aitzos/ch01" class="start-reading">Start Reading →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .book-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem; }
